{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# Hard-remove the deprecated `resolved_statuses` config keys\n\nRemoval half of task [rebar:549c-032f-6cb0-4258], which decided DEPRECATE-not-remove and\nexecuted the deprecation half (change 1670). It was blocked on operator sign-off because\nremoving a documented operator-facing config key is a user-visible surface change.\n\n**OPERATOR SIGN-OFF IS GIVEN** (2026-08-12, verbatim: \"delete the old config settings is\napproved\"; provenance recorded in the first comment on this ticket). This is the fourth\nchange of the pre-1.0 breaking window that also landed tickets 97d4 and 6cc4.\n\n## Background\n\n`jira.resolved_statuses` fed the inbound absence probe (`adapters/jira/probe.py::\n_resolve_resolved_statuses`), reachable as recently as shipped v0.10.1; the probe went with\ntask f020 and 549c removed the write-only transport plumbing. Both keys are now **inert** —\naccepted, coerced and validated, read by nothing. Resolved/unresolved discrimination is\noutbound-owned (ADR 0028), so there is **no replacement setting**: operators simply delete\nthe line.\n\n## Plan (line numbers against origin/main @ abf3817187)\n\n### 1. `src/rebar/_config_schema.py` — delete the fields and coercers\n\n* Delete `ReconcilerConfig.resolved_statuses` (L465) with its 5-line DEPRECATED comment\n  block and `# read-via:` marker (L460-464).\n* Delete `JiraConfig.resolved_statuses` (L489) with its 5-line comment block and\n  `# read-via:` marker (L484-488).\n* Delete the two `_as_str_list` coercer entries: `reconciler` section L696, `jira`\n  section L706.\n* Check `_as_str_list` for other callers; if this removes its last one, delete the helper\n  too rather than leave a dead coercer.\n\n### 2. `src/rebar/_deprecations.py` — swap deprecation rows for tombstones\n\n* Delete the two `_scheduled(\"cfg\", …)` rows (L106-107) and the 549c comment block that\n  introduces them (L91-105).\n* Append a historical NOTE in the \"removed scheduled surfaces\" block recording\n  **operator-approved removal, 2026-08-12**, matching the wording pattern of the\n  neighbouring 97d4 / 6cc4 NOTEs.\n* Add to `_TOMBSTONE_REGISTRY`, in the existing `cfg, warn` group:\n  `_tomb(\"cfg\", \"jira.resolved_statuses\", \"\", \"warn\")` and\n  `_tomb(\"cfg\", \"reconciler.resolved_statuses\", \"\", \"warn\")`.\n* Add the auto-derived env twins to the `env, warn` group:\n  `_tomb(\"env\", \"REBAR_JIRA_RESOLVED_STATUSES\", \"\", \"warn\")` and\n  `_tomb(\"env\", \"REBAR_RECONCILER_RESOLVED_STATUSES\", \"\", \"warn\")` — env names derive\n  generically as `REBAR_<SECTION>_<KEY>` (config.py L273), so both were real usable inputs.\n  This follows the `REBAR_CODE_HEALTH_ENABLED` precedent.\n\n**Tombstone class is `warn`, deliberately.** `_deprecations.py` codifies the rule: `error`\nfor an operationally load-bearing removed input (store location, write/sync gate, auth,\nsecurity, lifecycle policy), `warn` for an inert one. These keys are inert — nothing reads\nthem and the behaviour they configured no longer exists — so a still-set key must not abort\nthe command. This matches every comparable cfg precedent (`code_health.enabled`,\n`code_health.analyzers`, `reconciler.lock_backend`, `reconciler.lock_max_retries`). It\ndeliberately does NOT follow 6cc4's `error` choice for `REBAR_LLM_MODEL`, whose stated\nrationale — \"silently ignoring a still-set model id would quietly change which model every\noperation runs\" — is a load-bearing argument that does not transfer to an inert key.\n\n### 3. Tests\n\n* `tests/unit/test_config_resolved_statuses_deprecation.py` — the whole module asserts the\n  deprecation semantics that no longer exist. Replace it with a removal module (mirroring\n  6cc4's `test_llm_model_env_deprecation.py` -> `test_llm_model_env_removal.py` rename)\n  asserting: the fields are gone from both dataclasses; a config still carrying either key\n  loads and warns rather than raising; the key is dropped from the parsed config; and the\n  env twins warn.\n* `tests/scripts/test_check_config_reads_heldout.py` L318-331 — the docstring and the\n  `assert all(\"resolved_statuses\" in r for r in reports)` assertion both encode the\n  now-deleted `# read-via:` markers. Retarget to whatever the config-read gate reports once\n  the markers are gone (expected: an empty report for these keys).\n* `tests/unit/test_deprecation_registry.py` L41 — comment references the 549c rows; update.\n\n### 4. Docs\n\n* `docs/config.md` — delete the `resolved_statuses` line (L285) and its 9-line DEPRECATED\n  comment block (L276-284) from the `[tool.rebar.jira]` sample.\n* `docs/user-guide.md` — delete the `resolved_statuses` row (L510) from the DC settings table.\n* `docs/release-notes.md` + `CHANGELOG.md` — add the removal entry alongside the sibling\n  pre-1.0 pass #3 entries.\n\n### 5. Gates\n\nRun the full local CI gate set from the worktree venv: the ten `check_*` gates, the six\ngenerators (regenerate all generated registries and commit the diff), and CI's pytest\ninvocation. Two specific risks: the **config-read gate** may flag orphaned `# read-via:`\nbookkeeping once the markers go, and the **module-size gate** — `_config_schema.py` sits at\n798/800, so this removal should pull it down; verify it does rather than assuming.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [x] operator sign-off for the removal is recorded on this ticket\n- [ ] both schema fields and their `_as_str_list` coercers are deleted\n- [ ] both keys are tombstoned warn-class, so an existing config still loads with a warning\n- [ ] the auto-derived env twins are tombstoned warn-class\n- [ ] the deprecation registry rows are gone and a historical NOTE records the\n      operator-approved 2026-08-12 removal\n- [ ] the `# read-via:` markers are gone and the heldout marker test matches\n- [ ] neither key is documented any more\n- [ ] all ten `check_*` gates, the six generators, `make lint`, `make typecheck` and CI's\n      pytest invocation are green; `Verified +1` before close"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786588673122362001,"uuid":"7a09ab3d-614f-473d-a9d4-0009133efc95"}